        "ru-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "f7a72ed9-19e2-38b1-bca1-1915f9eed7cf",
                "word": "подчас",
                "pos": "adv",
                "lang_code": "ru",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "385708b9-c46c-37b8-a589-678964357407",
                        "entry_id": "f7a72ed9-19e2-38b1-bca1-1915f9eed7cf",
                        "glosses": [
                            "книжн. иногда"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ccc1f26b-36b1-4f1b-b5ba-0798e981bfae",
                                "sense_id": "385708b9-c46c-37b8-a589-678964357407",
                                "text": "Все народы имеют свои национальные слабости; и если говорить правду, то подчас наша скромность, право, не лучше французского самохвальства."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b84121c0-8f01-400a-bff7-d4f15deeee22",
                                "sense_id": "385708b9-c46c-37b8-a589-678964357407",
                                "text": "Много, очень много тяжелого и трагического подчас бывает в жизни матроса."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "765260f8-a35e-4e73-8a00-41c74279f796",
                        "source_entry_id": "f7a72ed9-19e2-38b1-bca1-1915f9eed7cf",
                        "source_sense_id": "385708b9-c46c-37b8-a589-678964357407",
                        "target_lang_word": "sometimes",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "sometimes",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0dd3f03e-6091-3c24-a1f7-ad73f6efda68",
                                        "entry_id": "6ea2c7e4-2fd6-383d-81a2-e5366c9381a5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "On some occasions, over some periods, or in certain circumstances, but not always."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eec4f805-14b1-4fc8-987b-7329df2490fd",
                                                "sense_id": "0dd3f03e-6091-3c24-a1f7-ad73f6efda68",
                                                "text": "Sometimes I sit and think, but mostly I just sit."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bf598915-2b5c-4912-af12-8074b71793c7",
                                                "sense_id": "0dd3f03e-6091-3c24-a1f7-ad73f6efda68",
                                                "text": "It is good that we sometimes be contradicted, and ill though of, and that we always bear it well, even when we deserve to be well spoken of : perfect peace and security cannot be had in this world."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cb74cc8a-5ef1-4a32-9cc9-ea0621e071a8",
                                                "sense_id": "0dd3f03e-6091-3c24-a1f7-ad73f6efda68",
                                                "text": "We made an odd party before the arrival of the Ten, particularly when the Celebrity dropped in for lunch or dinner. He could not be induced to remain permanently at Mohair because Miss Trevor was at Asquith, but he appropriated a Hempstead cart from the Mohair stables and made the trip sometimes twice in a day."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e4a23dd4-79e2-4200-8aa0-03dd3d25db03",
                                                "sense_id": "0dd3f03e-6091-3c24-a1f7-ad73f6efda68",
                                                "text": "The solitary, lumbering trolls of Scandinavian mythology would sometimes be turned to stone by exposure to sunlight. Barack Obama is hoping that several measures announced on June 4th will have a similarly paralysing effect on their modern incarnation, the patent troll."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e74bfba5-d62f-43c4-9323-ac8968bdd579",
                                                "sense_id": "0dd3f03e-6091-3c24-a1f7-ad73f6efda68",
                                                "text": "In 16th and 17th century Britain, for example, women’s alopecia was sometimes interpreted as retribution for sins, including adultery."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a095bc6b-5f19-3d28-9118-c736dcf5f513",
                                        "entry_id": "6ea2c7e4-2fd6-383d-81a2-e5366c9381a5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "On a certain occasion in the past; once."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable",
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9fb81752-8eb2-4407-9212-546018b7df90",
                                                "sense_id": "a095bc6b-5f19-3d28-9118-c736dcf5f513",
                                                "text": "For yee were sometimes darkenesse, but now are yee light in the Lord: walke as children of light […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0ff1dba2-c69e-4ab8-8ec7-4aa480cd2c97",
                                                "sense_id": "a095bc6b-5f19-3d28-9118-c736dcf5f513",
                                                "text": "What art thou that vſurp’ſt this time of night, / Together with that Faire and Warlike forme / In which the Maieſty of buried Denmarke / Did ſometimes march : By Heauen I charge thee ſpeake."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "53022942-3463-47b5-8dd3-abed023139a9",
                                                "sense_id": "a095bc6b-5f19-3d28-9118-c736dcf5f513",
                                                "text": "They detract, ſcoffe and raile ſaith one, & barke at mee on every ſide, but I, like that Albanian dog ſometimes given to Alexander for a preſent, vindico me ab illis ſolo contemptu, I ly ſtill and ſleep, vindicate my ſelfe by contempt alone."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "sometimes",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f1141947-172d-386e-8bd2-bd5033a7dc3a",
                                        "entry_id": "47a80a11-e1d7-3693-a6ae-98d72990837e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Former; sometime."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable",
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a701386e-ab92-4490-83c2-d25b5cfefa39",
                                                "sense_id": "f1141947-172d-386e-8bd2-bd5033a7dc3a",
                                                "text": "Farewell old Gaunt, thy ſometimes brothers wife / With her companion Greefe, muſt end her life."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "77d22990-4d4d-4f7f-aad8-5d9f24cc2e42",
                        "source_entry_id": "f7a72ed9-19e2-38b1-bca1-1915f9eed7cf",
                        "source_sense_id": "385708b9-c46c-37b8-a589-678964357407",
                        "target_lang_word": "at times",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "at times",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cfb028a8-1233-3da5-ad21-f61c7661945a",
                                        "entry_id": "bab458c8-7e21-3441-b1bd-d26be6edf6d6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "On occasion, sometimes."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "idiomatic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "35c36cef-8a9b-4045-b58a-ba85069dd09f",
                                                "sense_id": "cfb028a8-1233-3da5-ad21-f61c7661945a",
                                                "text": "I feel lonely at times, but then somebody phones, or calls round, and I cheer up again."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "91cf614b-79ed-47ae-8518-fc4711a4b6d5",
                                                "sense_id": "cfb028a8-1233-3da5-ad21-f61c7661945a",
                                                "text": "She is popular with passengers as an all-weather vessel, but rather the reverse with yachtsmen as she has at times proved somewhat unwieldy, and certainly takes up a good deal of space in the narrow channels."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "97b01e70-ee60-46b0-b1fd-4e7602e9f3e2",
                                                "sense_id": "cfb028a8-1233-3da5-ad21-f61c7661945a",
                                                "text": "If at times Van Gaal’s players let themselves down with careless concessions of possession, Carver knew his side had been reprieved when, back to goal, Wayne Rooney controlled the ball on his chest, swivelled and dinked a shot wide."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7aff28c2-b24d-4cf9-ae73-ffd8884db229",
                                                "sense_id": "cfb028a8-1233-3da5-ad21-f61c7661945a",
                                                "text": "This means, at times, long and perhaps overly discursive discussions of other taxa."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1ba97781-691c-4fcb-9671-c8d873c2177e",
                        "source_entry_id": "f7a72ed9-19e2-38b1-bca1-1915f9eed7cf",
